# requirements/stellar/oort-1932.ears
capability: Oort 1932 vertical force rerun
owner: stellar
requirements:
  - id: STL-025
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall report Oort's 1932 formula constants, shape factors, slope of the force, flat-layer density, plateau force, density units and Table 14 integral as recomputed from his inputs, each beside the printed figure."
    rationale: "Every figure is read from the uploaded scan of BAN 6, 249 and recomputed, never replaced; a difference is reported, not asserted (docs/protocols/uc05-oort-1932.md, part A)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_oorts_arithmetic_is_recomputed_beside_his_printed_figures"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_density_from_a_slope_takes_off_the_rotation_term"
  - id: STL-026
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall select UC-05 tracers with the predeclared quality cuts, absolute-magnitude group, cylinder radius, latitude floor and parallax zero-point, and divide their counts by the column's exact volume about the plane it finds from the two hemispheres."
    rationale: "The column is a cone near the Sun and a cylinder beyond it; the per-file reduction of the bulk read must never drop a star some scenario uses, and a star without a radial velocity still counts toward the density."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_column_volume_is_a_cone_then_a_cylinder_and_odd_in_z"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_every_star_a_scenario_uses_survives_the_per_file_reduction"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_shared_cuts_keep_a_star_without_a_radial_velocity_in_the_density"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_suns_height_is_found_from_the_two_hemispheres"
  - id: STL-027
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall apply Oort's formula (7) to binned tracer densities and error-corrected mean square vertical velocities, and report the slope near the plane, the flattening over 200 to 500 pc, the plateau force and the local density, with Monte Carlo errors."
    rationale: "Synthetic isothermal tracers in a self-gravitating sheet and in a uniform slab fix the signs, the units, the Poisson rotation term and the bias of a straight line over 0 to 200 pc."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_a_self_gravitating_sheet_gives_its_slope_and_flattens"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_a_uniform_slab_gives_its_slope_and_does_not_flatten"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_radial_velocity_error_is_taken_off_the_mean_square"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_too_few_stars_is_a_named_failure"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_clipping_drops_a_runaway_from_its_bin_only_when_on"
  - id: STL-028
    pattern: event
    text: "When a UC-05 run completes, the stellar module shall read UC05-H1 only if every scenario's force flattens by the declared rule, read UC05-H0 only if no scenario's force flattens and every one rises, and read inconclusive otherwise."
    rationale: "A failed scenario or a baseline-only quick look decides nothing; the comparison with Oort's 0.092 Msun/pc3 and Table 14 is reported beside the verdict and never changes it."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_verdict_follows_the_planted_force"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_oorts_density_is_compared_with_the_local_density"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_a_failed_scenario_or_a_quick_look_decides_nothing"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_oort1932::test_the_report_sets_gaia_beside_table_14"
  - id: STL-029
    pattern: event
    text: "When `sdp oort1932 run` is invoked, the system shall read the density from the complete bulk Gaia copy or a given Parquet file and the velocities from the rvs subset or a given Parquet file, and write report.json and report.md."
    rationale: "Leigh runs UC-05 on the PC's bulk copy and rvs subset; without velocities the run says how to build them, and the export of both column samples becomes the recorded known-answer test."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_oort1932::test_the_arithmetic_needs_no_data"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_oort1932::test_a_run_without_velocities_says_how_to_build_them"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_oort1932::test_a_run_reads_the_density_from_the_bulk_copy_and_the_velocities_from_its_rvs_subset"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_oort1932::test_the_export_writes_both_samples_and_they_run_from_parquet"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_oort1932::test_a_column_with_no_star_passing_the_cuts_reports_a_failed_baseline"
